WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.297
The most important distinction is project versus product instance.

2
00:00:04.297 --> 00:00:07.552
CVA6 is the repository and configurable code base.

3
00:00:07.552 --> 00:00:12.760
The documentation says the repository as-is is not one specific production core.

4
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.294
A name such as C V thirty two A six zero X points to configuration-specific evidence.

5
00:00:18.294 --> 00:00:25.325
That evidence can define instruction extensions, privilege modes, interfaces, issue direction, and maturity.

6
00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:31.575
A feature found in one configuration should never be copied automatically to every CVA6 variant.

